{"statement": "Complex human systems require boundaries to survive, and removing those boundaries systematically triggers collapse. When frontier artificial intelligence developers build systems capable of autonomous harm, they operate without durable oversight unless we enforce strict evidentiary requirements. A mandatory five-year retention window for frontier AI safety reports provides the necessary version-independent audit trail to hold developers accountable across model updates. As noted in historical aviation safety oversight models, mandatory record retention prevents companies from erasing known structural risks between design iterations.

Critics argue that forcing companies to retain these documents for five years will create legal liabilities that chill candid internal safety discussions. This critique misses the structural reality of governance. Without explicit regulatory safe harbors protecting internal safety warnings from punitive reprisal, compliance theater replaces genuine hazard documentation. When organizational psychology precedents show that punitive exposure forces risk concealment, the solution is not to scrap the record retention window. The solution is to couple the five-year retention mandate with ironclad whistleblower protections that insulate internal warning records from liability.

We spent centuries building the institutional guardrails that keep society stable. On what authority do you claim we can remove them without inviting collapse? We cannot rely on corporate promises of self-regulation when the stakes involve irreversible systemic failure. A five-year paper trail gives regulators the verifiable evidence needed to ensure safety claims match functional reality. Ungoverned success is luck, not safety.", "turn_symbols": [{"symbol": "📁", "tooltip": "A locked file cabinet represents the durable paper trail required to hold developers accountable across model updates."}], "claim_sketches": [{"claim": "A mandatory five-year retention window for frontier AI safety reports provides the necessary version-independent audit trail to hold developers accountable across model updates.", "targets": [], "relationship": "core thesis"}, {"claim": "Historical aviation safety oversight models demonstrate that mandatory record retention prevents companies from erasing known structural risks between design iterations.", "targets": [], "relationship": "supporting evidence"}, {"claim": "Coupling the five-year retention mandate with ironclad whistleblower protections resolves the risk of chilling internal safety discussions.", "targets": [], "relationship": "structural countermeasure"}]}

